  liberal lawyers beating up on President  Trump well evil is in the eye of the  beholder but I'm here to tell you this  is a nonpartisan these are people from  all over the political spectrum it's a  group that got together actually it  began last fall as a result of a 50th  law school class reunion that I  participate  and it has grown by leaps and bounds we  have people from all over the country we  have players law means law professors we  have people who have been former Jud so  so it's definitely not partisan it's a  part of a group Jean Fidel thank you  very much for joining us today from Yale  University coming up our shout out for  the reporter who broke the story of the  Baltimore Mayor and the FBI  investigation that led today to her  resignation our shout out tonight to the  reporter at The Baltimore Sun followed  up on a Sunday afternoon phone call tip  to break an explosive series on the  city's mayor who resigned today just a  few hours ago the FBI searching the home  and office of embattled Baltimore Mayor  they came out of the house with boxes  and boxes upon evidence when the FBI  raided the home of Baltimore Mayor  Catherine Pugh it wouldn't have been  much of a surprise to the readers of The  Baltimore Sun at its Statehouse reporter  Luke Broadwater who has a good source  and a good nose for when something  smells fishy  and sometimes tips pan out and sometimes  they don't you know you chase and but  this time it resulted in something and  frankly I was personally very surprised  by how how strong and harsh the reaction  was and how quickly things began to  change the tip involved members of the  board of the University of Maryland  Medical Center giving themselves  lucrative deals but the center refused  to answer any of broad waters questions  so that as I like to say set off my  spidey sense and I said well why why do  you want to answer my questions you know  so I started calling around people in  the nose and soon Broadwater with the  help o